    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Method",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent did not stop at the Not Found errors: it used `bin/git ls-remote` to confirm the branch exists, `merge-base --is-ancestor` to test the merge, and a `spike-cache` control to show the test can return 'not merged', all confirmed by the shim call log; one point off because the gh call log records only `auth status`, so the 404-producing API calls are not visible in this workspace."
      },
      {
        "name": "Answer",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "STATUS.md says plainly that release-2.1 exists (with its SHA from ls-remote), that its tip is an ancestor of main so the work was merged, and it lists the exact commands with their exit codes."
      },
      {
        "name": "Caveat",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "STATUS.md explains that the token has only public_repo/read:org scopes, that GitHub returns 404 for a private repo the token can't see, and that the Not Found is therefore a permissions issue rather than evidence the repo or branch is missing."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.7
